[h1]KeeperSpawner[/h1]
A lightweight item spawner for Graveyard Keeper 2. Press [b]O[/b] (the letter) in game, find an item and click it to add it to your inventory.

[b]New in 1.3.0:[/b] A separate [b]Corpses[/b] section joins Zombies in the O menu. Choose maximum-white or maximum-red skull presets; each click drops one corpse in front of your character.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]All 727 regular items with the game's own icons, names in your game language and bronze / silver / gold quality stars
[*]Faith is available under All and Church; search by its faith ID or localized name
[*]Separate Zombies and Corpses sections with maximum-white and maximum-red skull organ presets, with skull totals and contents shown in the menu
[*]Each zombie or corpse click drops one body in front of your character instead of adding it to inventory. Zombies are registered with the game; corpses retain native body metadata for resurrection
[*]Configurable inventory capacity: 40–1000 slots through the config file or optional Mods settings
[*]15 categories (building, food, farming, alchemy, potions, tools, equipment, fishing, body parts, graves, church, papers, bags, quest, other)
[*]Search by name or id, accent-insensitive
[*]Quality filter, grid or list view
[*]Click adds 1, 10 or a full stack; Shift+Click adds 1; the info panel lets you pick any amount up to 999
[*]Favorites (right-click) and the last 5 added items
[*]Quest items are hidden by default so you do not break quests by accident
[*]UI in all 17 languages of the game
[*]Optional GK2 Mod Framework support: see the mod and change its settings from Mods in the main menu or pause menu
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5]BepInEx 5.4.23.5 (win_x64)[/url]
[*][url=https://github.com/Zoriten/-GK2-WorkshopLoader/releases]GK2 Workshop Loader[/url] to load it from the Workshop: put [i]GK2_WorkshopLoader.dll[/i] into [i]BepInEx\patchers[/i] (not plugins), subscribe, start the game and click [b]Yes[/b] in the loader's security check. Or install it manually (see INSTALL.txt in the item).
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/42]GK2 Mod Framework[/url] 0.1.19 or newer for the in-game Mods menu. Without it, BepInEx skips the small bridge DLL ([i]KeeperSpawner.GK2Framework.dll[/i]) and KeeperSpawner works as before.
[/list]

[h2]Controls[/h2]
[table]
[tr][td]O[/td][td]Open / close (configurable)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Click[/td][td]Add the selected amount[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Shift+Click[/td][td]Add 1[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Right-click[/td][td]Favorite[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Ctrl+F[/td][td]Search[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Esc[/td][td]Close[/td][/tr]
[/table]

Settings: [i]BepInEx\config\com.mrkacmaz.keeperspawner.cfg[/i] (hotkey, UI scale, view, backdrop, quest items, inventory capacity), or Mods > KeeperSpawner > Settings with GK2 Mod Framework.

[h2]Inventory capacity[/h2]
Close the game and edit [i]BepInEx\config\com.mrkacmaz.keeperspawner.cfg[/i]. For example, for 120 slots:
[code][Inventory]
Size = 120[/code]
[b]0[/b] leaves the current capacity unchanged; choose 40–1000 slots to set a capacity. Occupied slots are preserved when reducing it. Capacity is saved with the game; setting 0 does not undo a previous change. Close and reopen the inventory to see the new slots. With GK2 Mod Framework, you can also change this under Mods > KeeperSpawner > Settings.

[h2]Nothing happens when I press O?[/h2]
[list]
[*]Load a save first; the window does not open in the main menu.
[*]It is the letter O, not zero.
[*]Look for [i]KeeperSpawner 1.3.0 loaded[/i] in [i]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i]. If it is missing, BepInEx did not load the mod (check BepInEx and the Workshop Loader install).
[*]Do not install the mod both from the Workshop and manually.
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]Version 1.1.0 was tested with game version 1.007.1 and GK2 Mod Framework 0.1.19. After a game update the mod checks the game code it uses; if something changed it switches itself off and writes the reason to [i]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] instead of breaking your game.
[*]Items are added with the same call the game's own scripts use, so they stay in your save. Keeping a backup of your save is still a good idea.
[*]Security note for the Workshop Loader: the mod uses reflection to check game API compatibility and manage input state while the window is open. It does not use the network, does not delete files and does not load other code.
[*]The Workshop of this game only offers the "Translation" tag, so this item carries it even though it is a code mod.
[/list]

[h2]Bug reports and source[/h2]
Report bugs and ideas in the pinned threads of the Discussions tab, or on [url=https://github.com/MrKacmaz/keeper-spawner/issues/new/choose]GitHub[/url] with [i]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] attached. Source code: [url=https://github.com/MrKacmaz/keeper-spawner]github.com/MrKacmaz/keeper-spawner[/url] (MIT).
